#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# own_values

#% text
# `own_values(x)` gives the value of the symbol `x` as a one-element list of a delayed rule `x :> value`, or the empty list when `x` has no value.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The symbol is held, so its value is read instead of substituted.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
x = 5

#% cell
own_values(x)
#% output
#= [x :> 5]

#% cell
own_values(not_a_symbol_with_a_value)
#% output
#= []

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `names`, `unset`
